// The same fn called from a const's body AND from the argument to that const.
// The expansion holds both, so the edge is collected twice - harmless, since
// edges are only used for reachability, cycles and max depth, and all three
// ignore duplicates.
//
// Unlike ok-const-body-calls-fn, this one compiled even before expansions were
// followed: the argument alone made `double` reachable. It is here for the
// emitter, which has to splice a call-bearing argument into a substitution and
// still evaluate it via the stack.

u16 double( u8 n ) => n * 2

const plusOne( u8 n ) = double( n ) + 1

u16 out
out = plusOne( u8( double( 2 ) ) )
